speechtext:
That, whereas the Constitution Act, 1867 provides in section 17 that there shall be one Parliament for Canada, consisting of the Queen, an Upper House styled the Senate and the House of Commons;
And whereas it is expedient that the electors of Canada be more directly involved in the legislative process;
And whereas an initiative and referendum process is an appropriate mechanism for the determination of questions of national interest;
And whereas the Parliament of Canada should be bound to enact any measures necessary to implement decisions of the electors of Canada on questions put to them by referendum;
Now, therefore, the House of Commons resolves that an amendment to the Constitution of Canada be authorized to be made by proclamation issued by His Excellency the Governor General under the Great Seal of Canada in accordance with the schedule hereto.
